  "term": "apolipoprotein E",
  "definition": "Apolipoprotein E is a protein involved in moving fats in the body and helping clear lipoproteins through low-density lipoprotein receptors. The packet describes three common forms, called ε2, ε3, and ε4, and notes that these genetic differences are linked to differences in cardiovascular disease risk.",
